// RUN CANARY (exit 70). Two modules each declare a boundary trait `Sink`
// whose requirement `emit` is resultless, a provider satisfying it, and a
// `Runner` whose `sink: Binding<Sink>` field is called as a statement in the
// entry state and again in a named state. A statement call through the field
// belongs to the requirement the field's declared type names. The entry is
// `right::Runner::run`, the later of the two same-spelled runners, so a
// lookup that took the first `Runner` by its spelling would read `left`'s
// field and name `left::Sink::emit`. Resolved exactly, the calls reach
// `right::Provider`, which writes each byte it receives: "R" from the entry
// state, then the newline from `deliver`, which exits 70. A call that
// crossed into `left::Sink::emit` runs `left::Provider`, which exits 66;
// `left`'s own runner would exit 65.
use left;
use right;
